      "problem": "$-2\\operatorname{log}⁡3+3\\operatorname{log}⁡3=$",
      "worked_solution": "Both logarithmic terms have a base of $10$ and an argument of $3.$ Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{log}⁡3+3\\operatorname{log}⁡3 & =(-2+3)\\operatorname{log}⁡3=\\operatorname{log}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
