    "q-66634": {
      "dom_id": "step-q66634",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $7{log}_{2}⁡3-{log}_{2}⁡3?$",
      "worked_solution": "Both logarithmic terms have a base of $2$ and an argument of $3.$ Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{log}_{2}⁡3-{log}_{2}⁡3 & =(7-1){log}_{2}⁡3=6{log}_{2}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
