    "q-108094": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108094",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $7\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)+5\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Both the first and the second logarithmic terms have a base of $10$ and an argument of $5x.$ Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)+5\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x) & =(7-2)\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)+5\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)+5\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
