    "q-24216": {
      "dom_id": "step-q24216",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$4{log}_{6}⁡(x)+3{log}_{6}⁡(2x)-12{log}_{6}⁡(x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "Both the first and the third logarithmic terms have a base of $6$ and an argument of $x.$ Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{log}_{6}⁡(x)+3{log}_{6}⁡(2x)-12{log}_{6}⁡(x) & =(4-12){log}_{6}⁡(x)+3{log}_{6}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =-8{log}_{6}⁡(x)+3{log}_{6}⁡(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
